  "_comment": "Learner-visible text → what the synthesizer is fed. The hash/cache key stays on the visible text (Job.text); only synthesis input changes. Class: sentence-initial ははは without punctuation reads as laughter (ha-ha-ha) — whisper-audited 2026-08-20, 5 of 16 shipped clips failed. All 16 are pinned so a forced regen can never re-roll the dice. Kanji 母 disambiguates (Spencer's pick, R17: kanji-fed generation, forced わ rejected).",
  "_comment2": "Class 2: elliptical 'Noun-は？' questions (TestFlight #9, 2026-09-06). Same root cause family — kana-only input starves the Azure front-end's word segmenter, so a sentence-final topic は with no following predicate reads as the syllable /ha/ instead of the particle /wa/. Fix mirrors class 1: feed the content noun in kanji, keep the ？ (getTtsUrl has no ？-stripping fallback — the question contour must survive). Swept every JA IR yaml for `<noun>は？`-shaped endings; entries below are the ones with an unambiguous, homophone-safe kanji (common N5/N4 vocab). NOT fixed here: sentence-final proper names (トムは？/ミカは？/ケンは？) and katakana loanwords (テレビは？) have no kanji lever — forcing わ into the speech text is permanently rejected (Spencer, R17, option F sounded 'weird'), so those stay open pending a phoneme/SSML mechanism this pipeline does not yet have.",
